; The poisoned bucket: the second declaration lost its name in a bad
; merge, and the scanner refuses the whole source rather than register
; the two names it *could* read (a truncated member set would mis-blame
; every reference that follows). The result is exactly one diagnostic,
; `cross_ref_extraction_failed` at the shader, and silence at both
; binds below: `u_time` would have resolved and `u_missing` would not,
; and neither is reported, because a member set nobody could compute has
; no answer to give. Unchecked is neither accepted nor rejected.
;
; `cross_ref_provider_unavailable` (a host that cannot run the provider
; at all) reaches the same silence by the other door.
(use-plugin "uniforms")

(shader :name sky :src """@group(0) @binding(0) var<uniform> u_time: f32;
@group(0) @binding(1) var<uniform> : f32;
@group(0) @binding(2) var<uniform> u_tint: vec4f;
""")

(bind :uniform u_time :group 0 :binding 0)
(bind :uniform u_missing :group 0 :binding 9)
